    <span class="eyebrow">Legal &amp; Trust Center</span>
    <h1>Client Confidentiality</h1>
    <p class="ld-sub">Discretion is part of how we work. Some of our most important work is never shown publicly &mdash; and that is by design.</p>
    <div class="ld-meta">Last updated: June 2026</div>
  </header>
  <article class="ld-body">
<section><h2><span class="n">01</span>A core principle</h2><p>Confidentiality is fundamental to the way BaseCamp Studio&reg; operates. The trust our clients place in us &mdash; often with sensitive strategy, unreleased products and market-moving launches &mdash; is something we protect without exception.</p></section>
<section><h2><span class="n">02</span>Work you will never see</h2><p>Many of our projects cannot be displayed publicly. Some portfolio work is intentionally omitted, and certain clients are never named. The absence of a project from our public work is a feature of our discretion, not a measure of its scale or success.</p></section>
<section><h2><span class="n">03</span>How we protect information</h2><ul><li>Confidential information is never shared outside the engagement.</li><li>Non-disclosure agreements are strictly respected.</li><li>Internal strategic materials remain confidential.</li><li>Access to sensitive work is limited to those who need it.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2><span class="n">04</span>Discretion as a standard</h2><p>For our clients, confidentiality is not a restriction &mdash; it is a guarantee. It is what allows us to do our most ambitious work, quietly, alongside the people who trust us with it.</p></section>
  </article>
